## Look hardest at
- The schema probe: does a store MISSING the column now actually fail the probe
  and trigger the migration retry (store.go:158-172)? That is the whole point —
  a probe that still passes converts a diagnosable startup error into a
  runtime read-path failure on every `GetIssue`/`SearchIssues`.
- The memory backend's `UpdateIssue` case: does it accept both a `*time.Time`
  value AND an explicit nil (clearing the lease)? A case that handles only the
  set direction leaves a lease that can never be cleared in `--no-db` mode.
- Does the memory backend's decision matrix now match the sqlite one, including
  the steal event carrying the prior holder?
- The schema constant: does it match what migration 027 produces, exactly? A
  drift between constant and migration is the defect being fixed, so an
  imprecise fix reintroduces it in a new place.
- Do the new tests fail if the fix is reverted? Say so explicitly in your
  verdict, and name any test that would pass either way.

